    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "##Investigate and Modify\r\n\r\nExperiment with the program by making the following modifications, then run the program to observe the results.\r\n\r\n✅ **TO DO:** Look at the <code style=\"background-color: #ececec; color: black; font-weight: bold;\">getGrade()</code> method in the <code style=\"background-color: #ececec; color: black; font-weight: bold;\">Teacher</code> class. What do the values in <code style=\"background-color: #ececec; color: black; font-weight: bold;\">weeklyGrades[row][col]</code> refer to?\r\n\r\nIn the <code style=\"background-color: #ececec; color: black; font-weight: bold;\">TeacherRunner</code> class, try changing the values in the call to the <code style=\"background-color: #ececec; color: black; font-weight: bold;\">getGrade()</code> method to access different elements in the 2D array <code style=\"background-color: #ececec; color: black; font-weight: bold;\">augustGrades</code>.",
    "mini_rubric": "false",
